        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0340" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1592</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1382</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my telegram of February 1,
                    1917, 1 p.m., I have the honor to enclose herewith for the information of the
                    Department a translation of a note (No. 560) from the Ministry of Foreign
                    Affairs, under date of the 7th instant, advising me of the designation of a line
                    from Chouchiakou (in Honan) through Nanyang to Hsiangyang (in Hupeh) for
                    construction under the terms of the Siems-Carey Company’s contracts of May 17
                    and September 29 last with the Chinese Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul S. Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d235-a1.xml" xpointer="d235-a1"/>
            </div>
